        <summary>
          <para>The operation failed because it is fundamentally incompatible with this device. For example, the app may require a hardware feature that doesn't exist, it may be missing native code for the ABIs supported by the device, or it requires a newer SDK version, etc. Starting in Build.VERSION_CODES.UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE, an app with only 32-bit native code can still be installed on a device that supports both 64-bit and 32-bit ABIs. However, a warning dialog will be displayed when the app is launched.</para>
